7. OBSERVATIONS (neither is a defect in this PR; both already reported on #804)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
(a) c.RealIP() trusts X-Forwarded-For from any client, because e.IPExtractor is
    never set in the repo. A node that sets the header writes whatever it wants,
    so the stored value is a display hint rather than an unspoofable
    server-observed fact unless AuroraBoot sits behind a trusted proxy. The same
    echo default already governs the per-client-IP registration rate limiter on
    main, so this predates this diff. Worth a follow-up about IPExtractor /
    trusted proxies.

(b) Agent-side, not AuroraBoot: when the address is removed out from under a
    live WebSocket, the agent keeps writing into the dead socket and heartbeats
    stall well past 60s, so the IP only refreshes once the connection actually
    drops. Reproduced again in this run:

      $ sudo ip netns exec qa4590 ss -tanp
        ESTAB 0 9152  10.99.0.2:42616  10.99.0.1:9990 users:(("qa4590-kairos-a",pid=1321452,fd=8))
      t+85s  remoteIP=10.99.0.2 phase=Offline
      t+320s remoteIP=10.99.0.2 phase=Offline     # still wedged, 5+ min
      agent log: no reconnect attempt logged at all

    Forcing the socket to drop (`ss -K`, or a real link flap / node reboot) makes
    the refresh land in under 5s, as section 3 shows. This is kairos-agent
    reconnect behaviour and does not affect AuroraBoot's acceptance criteria.

